F6 driver review. close_march.py = WAVE2/F2/close_march.py plus one guard (diff at the end).
Checked against WAVE1/W19/scripts/close_march.py (F2/driver.diff is the W19 -> F2 diff):
(a) fresh directory per job: solve() uses tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="s_<k>_", dir=WORK) and march()
    uses tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="m_<tag>_", dir=WORK); both removed after use. No shared s_k names
    (AUDIT RISK-3b). WORK=/opt/work/tmp, used only by this one driver process.      OK
(b) finalize() writes leaves.icnf and open.icnf with tempfile.mkstemp in OUTDIR, then os.replace
    (AUDIT RISK-1).                                                                    OK
(c) when leaves.jsonl does not exist, the first record written is {"case": NAME, "case_sha256": sha
    of the case CNF}; checked in U_L8/leaves.jsonl line 1 (U_L8, 6c05114f...).        OK
Also: leaves.icnf holds only records with status UNSAT and cake_lpr == "s VERIFIED UNSAT" (AUDIT
BUG-1); other cake verdicts become UNSAT_UNCHECKED and stay open. SKIP records (cubes listed in
--skip, built by mkskip.py from others' verified leaves) count as closed for open.icnf but are
never written to leaves.icnf. leaves.jsonl did not exist before this run (no stale records, RISK-3c).
Case CNF sha checked by hand before the run (6c05114f... = cases.jsonl); the driver records it.
F6 change: if march_cu returns no cubes or an empty cube (refuted, `a 0`), the child would equal
the parent and loop forever (AUDIT NOTE-1); such a record gets status SPLIT_FAIL and the cube stays open.

